<!doctype html>
<html lang="en" data-marble="1">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<meta name="marble:capabilities" content="storage; net=none">
<title>__TITLE__</title>
<style>
  /* The Marble design system's palette, with one change the system does not
     make: a document is white to the edge. The off-white paper belongs to
     the interface — the Drive itself — not to the thing you are writing in.
     One dusty blue does all the accenting, the same blue in every starter,
     because five colours would be five claims and there is only one. */
  :root {
    --ink: #111111;
    --muted: #5a5a5a;
    --line: #ddd9cf;
    --paper: #ffffff;
    --card: #ffffff;
    --accent: #9bb6cf;
    --accent-soft: #f1f5f8;
    --accent-ink: #738698;
  }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    :root {
      --ink: #e8e6e1; --muted: #a3a7ab; --line: #2f3438;
      --paper: #1c1f22; --card: #1c1f22;
      --accent: #7fa8c9; --accent-soft: #1d2932; --accent-ink: #9dc0dc;
    }
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body {
    margin: 0; padding: 3.5rem 1.5rem 8rem;
    background: var(--paper); color: var(--ink);
    font: 16px/1.7 -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif;
    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
  }
  .page {
    max-width: 46rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 3.5rem 4rem 4rem;
    background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 8px;
  }
  h1 { font-size: 2rem; line-height: 1.2; margin: 0 0 .35rem; letter-spacing: -.02em; }
  .lede { color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 2.5rem; font-size: 1.05rem; }
  .sections { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  .section { padding: .35rem 0 1.4rem; }
  .section h2 { font-size: 1.15rem; margin: 0 0 .4rem; letter-spacing: -.01em; }
  .section p { margin: 0 0 .7rem; }
  [data-marble-editable] { outline: none; border-radius: 3px; }
  [data-marble-editable]:hover { background: var(--accent-soft); }
  [data-marble-editable]:focus { background: var(--card); box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px var(--accent), 0 0 0 4px var(--accent-soft); }
  .add {
    appearance: none; display: block; width: 100%; margin-top: .5rem; padding: .6rem;
    border: 1px dashed var(--line); border-radius: 6px; background: none;
    color: var(--muted); font: 500 .9rem/1 inherit; cursor: pointer;
  }
  .add:hover { color: var(--accent-ink); border-color: var(--accent); }
  @media (max-width: 40rem) { .page { padding: 2rem 1.5rem; } }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<article class="page" data-marble-id="__ID__">

  <h1 data-marble-id="__ID__" data-marble-editable>__TITLE__</h1>
  <p class="lede" data-marble-id="__ID__" data-marble-editable>Type over anything on this page. Drag a section by the handle on its left. What you see is the file.</p>

  <ol class="sections" data-marble-id="__ID__" data-marble-sortable="sections">
    <li class="section" data-marble-id="__ID__" data-marble-removable>
      <h2 data-marble-id="__ID__" data-marble-editable>The first section</h2>
      <p data-marble-id="__ID__" data-marble-editable>There is no save button, because there is nothing to save — the change you just made is the file on disk. Open this document in a text editor and you will find this sentence in it.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="section" data-marble-id="__ID__" data-marble-removable>
      <h2 data-marble-id="__ID__" data-marble-editable>The second section</h2>
      <p data-marble-id="__ID__" data-marble-editable>Sections reorder by dragging the handle, or by focusing it and pressing the arrow keys. Either way the move is a single edit to the file, and undo is the same move backwards.</p>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <button class="add" data-marble-transient data-marble-add="#tpl-section" data-marble-into="prev">+ section</button>

</article>

<template id="tpl-section" data-marble-transient>
  <li class="section" data-marble-removable>
    <h2 data-marble-editable>New section</h2>
    <p data-marble-editable>Say something here.</p>
  </li>
</template>

__SCRIPT__
</body>
</html>
